# The Kentucky index slices are the year files' own bytes, CRLF line ends and carriage-control bytes included: never normalised.
ky-*.txt -text
# The New Jersey index lines are the file's own, line feeds only: never normalised.
nj-*.csv -text
# A saved response is the holder's own bytes, whatever its line ends (the gravesite locator's pages end their lines with CRLF):
# never normalised, so each is still the archive's object, byte for byte.
va-*.html -text
ia-*.json -text
nara-*.json -text
wikidata-*.json -text
wikitree-*.json -text
geocoder/*.json -text
